    "body": "BMW overhauled its flagship i7 electric sedan. Now, it wants you to use it as a chauffeur vehicle.\nBMW launches i7 chauffeur program in the UK\nThe 7 Series sits atop BMW’s sedan lineup as its flagship sedan, including its all-electric counterpart, the i7.\nAs part of BMW’s revamped lineup, which will include 40 new or refreshed models through 2027, BMW introduced the new 7 Series and i7 earlier this year.\nThe flagship sedan “takes the lead when it comes to the introduction of technologies from the Neue Klasse into existing models,” BMW said.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nUnlike the new iX3 and i3, which are ground-up Neue Klasse EVs, the new i7 retains its classic flagship design with a modern twist.\nAlthough it still has BMW’s massive kidney grille, it features a slightly smaller version with available “Kidney Iconic Glow.” It also has a new minimalist crystal headlights that replace the outgoing i7’s stacked headlight design.\nInside, the i7 adopts BMW’s Neue Klasse design and technology with plenty of digital screens. The setup includes a 17.9″ floating center infotainment display, BMW’s Panoramic Vision spanning the dashboard, and a 14.6″ passenger entertainment screen.\nIt’s powered by the latest BMW Operating System X, which includes an in-car intelligent assistant with Amazon Alexa+ AI technology.\nThe rear passengers get an upgraded 31.3″ 8K BMW Theatre Screen that drops down from the roof to watch movies or work on the go. Other premium features include new ambient lighting, updated automatic doors, and a digital interior mirror.\nTo make longer road trips more comfortable, the new i7 features ergonomically designed seats and standard adaptive 2-axle air suspension.\nLike the iX3, the new i7 uses BMW’s sixth-generation (Gen6) eDrive. The 113 kWh battery provides up to 447 miles (720 km) of WLTP range. In the US, BMW estimates the 2027 i7 will offer up to 362 miles of EPA range.\nSounds like it would make a good Chauffeur vehicle. BMW UK launched a dedicated Chauffeur Program using the new 7 Series and electric i7.\nThe program is designed to reduce downtime and help professional chauffeurs grow their business with tailored solutions.\nBMW’s program includes Service Inclusive, a five-year service plan covering unlimited mileage for the new 7 Series and i7. It also includes a one-year subscription to BMW Security PRO, a 24/7 vehicle protection and tracking system to safeguard the vehicle.\nAs part of the program, BMW is also offering Mobility Support, which lets drivers use a licensed replacement or receive support during warranty repairs. It also includes BMW’s high-voltage battery warranty for up to eight years or 100,000 miles.\nFor those who place an eligible BMW i7 Chauffeur Program order by the end of 2026, BMW is throwing in a free Pod home charger.\nThe program is available through BMW retailers across the UK and open to licensed private hire operators, chauffeur companies, executive transport providers, luxury hotel house-car fleets, corporate and VIP transport operators, and self-employed chauffeurs. However, BMW said the program is not available to taxi operators.\nBMW does not offer a direct Chauffeur program in the US, but the 2027 BMW i7 50 xDrive is now on sale, starting at $106,200. The more powerful i7 60 xDrive starts at $124,700.\nReady to see one in person? We can help you get started. You can use our link here to find available 2027 BMW i7s and other vehicles near you.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
